        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "07cd9956-6658-5c07-9030-4aea47b68754",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Achel Abbey, Orval Abbey, Cistercians of Strict Observance\n- Places: Achel, Campine, Limburg, Flanders, Belgium, Netherlands, Austria, Italy, United States\n- Products: Trappist beer, Authentic Trappist Product, Orval, cheese\n- Topics: spiritual life, breweries, Trappist monasteries\n\nFacts:\n- Achel Abbey, also called Saint Benedictus-Abbey or Achelse Kluis, belongs to the Cistercians of Strict Observance.\n- Achel Abbey is located in Achel in the Campine region of Limburg in Flanders, Belgium.\n- Achel Abbey is known for its spiritual life and for its brewery, which is one of the few Trappist beer breweries in the world.\n- Eleven monasteries currently brew beer sold as \"Authentic Trappist Product\": six in Belgium, two in the Netherlands, and one each in Austria, Italy, and the United States.\n- Orval Abbey is known for its history and spiritual life and for producing the Trappist beer Orval and a specific cheese.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
